The meshes in this folder are built from NASA's OpenVSP model of its Quiet Single Main Rotor helicopter, 450 ft/s
design (file QEU2023-SMR-6pax-turbo-notar_450fps.vsp3, sha256
1a9b3940a1e021fa0b345575d50386a6a186b47615ec4cc9fea19747da4f9da1, in
https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/qsmr-vsp.zip, sha256
c9909b05206bcf04193c99eeb74ae1ffa6521db4955b4b1b86da8fc89617a13a). The model is a work of NASA's Revolutionary
Vertical Lift Technology project; under the NASA media usage guidelines (nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media)
NASA's 3D model files "generally are not subject to copyright in the United States". NASA is acknowledged here and
does not endorse PteroSim. No NASA insignia, logotype or identifier appears on the meshes or their textures.

Changes made here (scripts/ holds the pipeline): the geometry was tessellated with OpenVSP 3.55 and split by
component; PteroLabs modelled the detail NASA's concept model leaves out (landing gear struts and torque links, the
exhaust, the direct-jet thruster's fixed and turning cones with their vanes), unwrapped the result, and painted and
baked its own textures: the livery, access panels, steps, the circulation-control slot and the lettering "Orca",
"PTEROSIM" and "PS-U1". body.glb is the airframe, rotor.glb the main rotor about its hub with the disc
level, thruster.glb the thruster's turning cone about its axis; all in NASA's frame (X aft, Y right, Z up, origin at
the rotor hub), metres.
